          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The term
            %em Grothendieck group
            has two closely related meanings:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OfCommutativeMonoids"} Grothendieck group of commutative monoids
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OfStableCategories"} Grothendieck group of stable infinity-categories
          %p
            In its restricted sense the Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid (i.e. of a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a specific presentation of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            it produces the additive group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            represented by pairs of natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_+, n_-)
            subject to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            such that the class of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_+, n_-)
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/difference"} difference
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_+ - n_-
          %p
            A vaguely similar procedure applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} isomorphism classes
            of objects in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"} Quillen exact category
            computes a group that is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of that category. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            for some general abstract nonsense behind this.
          %p
            Notably, the Grothendieck group completion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            on some (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"}> compact Hausdorff
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            produces the group known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Given this one speaks more generally of the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"}> algebraic
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            group of a suitable category (one presenting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            in some way) as its
            %em Grothendieck group
            \.
          %p
            In that sense, the Grothendieck group of a (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-)category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a notion of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} cofibration sequence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
            equipped with a notion of addition that is encoded in these homotopy exact sequences.
          %p
            We now first state the definition of “Grothendieck group completion” – which is really just the
            %em
              free group completion of an abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            – and then the definition of Grothendieck group in the sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
          %h2#OfCommutativeMonoids Of commutative monoids
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            is in particular a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo →
                  %mi CMon
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon Ab \to CMon
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            to the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon"} CMon
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (the corresponding
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free functor
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi F
                  %mi CMon
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ab
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{U}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{F}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  CMon
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+construction+on+commutative+monoids"} Grothendieck group construction on commutative monoids
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct"}
            below) is an explict presentation of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            functor.
          %p
            For more details see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The idea of the free group on an abelian monoid is a very simple algebraic idea that, at least for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative monoid
              (so that the unit is monic and one can reasonably use the term ‘completion’) certainly predates
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is the group completion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              goes back at least to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker"} Kronecker
          #GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"}> Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,+)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              (i.e. a commutative
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of underlying sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times A
              (the set of ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of elements in
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mi k
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+, a_-) \sim_1 (b_+, b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{k \in A}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    a_+ + b_- + k = b_+ + a_- + k
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
            %p or equivalently the equivalence relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+, a_-) \sim_2 (b_+, b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{k_1, k_2 \in A}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    (a_+ + k_1, a_- + k_1)
                    \=
                    (b_+ + k_2, b_- + k_2)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G(A) \coloneqq (A \times A)/\sim
            %p
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              under this equivalence relation. This inherits a binary operation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    + \;\colon\; G(A) \times G(A) \longrightarrow G(A)
            %p
              by applying the addition in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on representatives:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [a_+,a_-] + [b_+,b_-] \coloneqq [ a_+ + b_+ , a_- + b_- ]
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (G(A),+)
            %p
              and this is the
              %em Grothendieck group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              This comes with a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroups"} semigroups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi A
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_A \phantom{A} }{\longrightarrow}&amp; G(A)
                    \\\
                    a &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; [a,0]
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h2#OfStableCategories
            Of stable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            In this sense, a Grothendieck group is fundamentally something assigned to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            classes of objects, which inherits the structure of an abelian monoid. Then in addition to group-completing it as above, we add additional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            by the rule that for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \to X \to B
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X]
            must satisfy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X] = [A] + [B]
                  \\,.
          %p
            The result is also called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            In particular, the additive inverse
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -[A]
            of an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            is the class of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} A
            called the
            %em suspension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega A \to 0 \to A
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \to 0 \to \Sigma A
          %p
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} fibration sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A] + [\Omega A] = 0
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [A] + [\Sigma A] = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            But there are many ways to
            %em model
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            by an ordinary category. Essentially for each of these ways there is a seperate prescription for how to model the above general construction in terms of concrete 1-categorical constructions.
          %p In particular from an
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p and a
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"} Quillen exact category
          %p
            one obtains the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} categories of chain complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            Apart from the case of abelian categories, this requires some handle on the fibration sequences. A tool developed to handle exactly this for the purpose of computing Grothendieck/K-theory groups is the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
          %h3#of_an_abelian_category of an abelian category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %strong Grothendieck group
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            group of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            generated by
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} isomorphism class
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X] = [A] + [B]
          %p
            whenever there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to A \to X \to B \to 0
          %h3#of_a_quillen_exact_category of a Quillen exact category
          %p
            An exact category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in the present sense is a full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            such that the collection of all sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to A \to X \to B \to 0
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            has the property that for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to X \to B
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in C
            also their “sum”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Given an exact category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with the inherited notion of exact sequences this way, the definition of its Grothendieck group is as above.
          %h3#of_a_waldhausen_category of a Waldhausen category
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            – called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            – and equipped with the notion of auxiliary morphism called
            = succeed "." do
              %em cofibrations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of a cofibration
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\to &amp;  B
                  }
          %p
            computes the desired
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %p
            Therefore in a Waldhausen category a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} cofibration sequence
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \hookrightarrow X \to B
          %p where the first morphism is a cofibration.
          %p
            The Grothendieck/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"}> K-theory
            \-group of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is then, as before, on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
            the abelian group structure given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X] = [A] + [B]
          %p for all cofibration sequences as above.
          %h3#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The Grothendieck group of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"} Quillen exact category
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is called the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %p
                Notice that vector bundles do not form an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %li
              %p
                The Grothendieck group of the category of finite-dimensional complex-linear
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                is called its
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
          %p
            These two examples illustrate a general fact: the Grothendieck group of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            inherits a ring structure from the tensor product in this category, and thus becomes a ring, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+ring"} Grothendieck ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
          %ul
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+category"} Quillen exact category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is canonically equipped with the structure of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Waldhausen+category"} Waldhausen category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
